# IndyShares Portfolio Builder
# Element Library, Asset System, Component & Template Library, and Global/Local Header & Footer
**Supplemental Product, UX, and Technical Specification**  
**Version:** 1.0  
**Status:** Proposed baseline for implementation  
**Document type:** Additive change specification

---

## 1. Purpose

This document extends the existing IndyShares Portfolio Builder specifications. It defines a richer Element Library, an asset workflow for icons and logos, reusable components and templates, and a per-page Header/Footer system with Global, Local, and None modes.

This is an additive specification. It does not replace the existing PRD, system design, page-management specification, responsive specification, or full CSS Property Editor specification. Where this document overlaps them, the established architecture remains authoritative.

### Product principles

1. The Builder must support real website construction, not only a small set of decorative blocks.
2. Elements, components, and templates must share one compatible document/component model.
3. Users must be able to save their own work for reuse without losing editability.
4. Global changes must have predictable scope; local changes must not unexpectedly modify other pages.
5. Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile behavior must be supported consistently.
6. User-owned portfolio source data and assets remain in the user's Google Workspace.
7. Supabase remains Authentication-only. Do not store portfolio, page, component, template, asset, or publishing records in Supabase.

