## 2. Terminology and object model

| Object | Definition | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Element | A basic insertable building block | Heading, Image, Button, Container |
| Component | A reusable composition of one or more elements | Profile Card, Navbar, Project Card |
| Section Template | A reusable section-level starting layout | Hero, Skills, Testimonials |
| Header Template | A reusable header composition | Main Header, Minimal Header |
| Footer Template | A reusable footer composition | Standard Footer, Compact Footer |
| Page Template | A starting layout for one page | About, Contact, Project Detail |
| Site Template | A starter website containing multiple pages and shared design | Portfolio starter site |
| Asset | A media or design file used by elements/components | SVG icon, logo, image, font |
| Global Component | A shared component referenced by multiple pages | Global Header |
| Local Component | A page-owned component instance or definition | Contact page custom header |

An Element is not automatically a Template. A selected group of elements can be saved as a Component or a Template through an explicit save action.

