## 3. Element Library

### 3.1 Panel requirements

Replace the current small, card-only element list with a searchable Element Library. The reference screenshot shows the existing panel pattern (search, insertion target, category chips, and element cards); retain the useful interaction model while expanding its coverage and visual clarity.

Required capabilities:

- Search by element name, description, category, and supported keywords.
- Category filters and optional subcategory filters.
- Icon-led element rows/cards with consistent iconography.
- Clear element name and short description.
- Drag-and-drop insertion.
- Click-to-insert as an accessible alternative to drag-and-drop.
- Insertion target controls: inside selected, after selected, and end of page, where applicable.
- Recently Used and Favorites.
- Built-in Elements and My Components/Templates.
- Preview or concise description before insertion for complex elements.
- Empty, loading, no-results, and error states.
- Keyboard navigation and visible focus states.
- Responsive panel behavior across Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile.

Do not use icons as the only accessible label. Every item must have a readable name and accessible description.

### 3.2 Recommended catalog

The catalog below is the minimum proposed coverage, not a hard limit. Avoid shipping duplicate elements that differ only by styling. Prefer a flexible base element with variants when behavior is genuinely the same.

| Category | Element examples |
|---|---|
| Layout | Container, Flex Container, Grid Container, Columns, Stack, Spacer, Divider, Section |
| Basic & Typography | Heading, Paragraph, Rich Text, Link, Button, List, Blockquote, Code, Label |
| Media | Image, Image Gallery, Video, Audio, Icon, Logo, Background Media, Embed |
| Navigation | Navbar, Navigation Menu, Breadcrumbs, Pagination, Anchor Link, Social Links |
| Forms & Interaction | Form, Text Input, Textarea, Select, Checkbox, Radio Group, Toggle, Modal, Tooltip, Tabs, Accordion |
| Portfolio | Profile, Project Card, Project Grid, Skills, Experience, Education, Timeline, Testimonials, Social Profile |
| Dynamic Data | Dynamic Text, Dynamic Image, Dynamic Link, Collection List, Repeater, Collection Grid, Data Table |
| Advanced | HTML, Custom CSS, Custom JavaScript, SVG, Lottie, Chart, Map, Custom Embed |

### 3.3 Element metadata

Each element definition should declare:

- Stable `elementType` identifier.
- Display name, description, category, keywords.
- Icon reference.
- Engine/component implementation identifier.
- Default properties and default child structure, if any.
- Supported child rules and nesting constraints.
- Content and style property schemas.
- Responsive property support.
- Accessibility defaults and requirements.
- Whether the element is safe for public rendering.
- Whether it supports dynamic data binding.
- Whether it is available in the current product tier, if tiering is later introduced.
- Version and migration metadata.

The Element Library must be metadata-driven. Do not hard-code each panel card independently from the underlying element registry.

### 3.4 Insertion and nesting

- Respect valid parent/child constraints.
- Show a clear insertion indicator before committing a drop.
- Prevent invalid nesting or explain why it is disallowed.
- Preserve selection and undo/redo behavior.
- When inserting a complex element, insert a valid editable component tree, not a flattened image or opaque HTML blob.
- Provide non-drag insertion and reorder controls for accessibility and touch devices.

