## 7. Responsive behavior

All Elements, Components, Templates, Headers, and Footers must use the existing Desktop / Tablet / Mobile responsive property model.

Requirements:
- One canonical component document with breakpoint-specific property overrides.
- Device preview does not create separate page/component copies.
- Explicit overrides inherit from larger breakpoints according to the existing responsive specification.
- Provide reset-to-inherited behavior.
- Header navigation must support mobile interaction patterns (e.g. menu toggle/drawer) without requiring hover.
- Touch targets, keyboard navigation, focus management, and accessible names are required.
- Local and Global Header/Footer must be previewable at all supported breakpoints.
- Template previews should expose device previews when responsive layout materially changes.

