## 8. UX flows

### 8.1 Insert an Element
1. Open Elements.
2. Search or browse a category.
3. Select an element.
4. Choose insertion target or drag it to a valid Canvas location.
5. Element appears selected and editable in the property panel.

### 8.2 Save selection as a Component/Template
1. Select one or more Canvas nodes.
2. Open Save as.
3. Choose the applicable type (Component, Section, Header, or Footer Template).
4. Enter name and optional description/tags.
5. Save to My Library.
6. Confirm the item is available in the relevant library category.

### 8.3 Create a Local Header from Global
1. Open Page Settings.
2. Set Header to Local.
3. Choose Copy current Global Header.
4. System creates an independent local component.
5. User edits it without affecting other pages.
6. Optionally save it as a Header Template.

### 8.4 Set a page to Global Header/Footer
1. Open Page Settings.
2. Set Header or Footer to Global.
3. System resolves the currently active global variant.
4. Editor shows a shared/global indicator.
5. Changes to that global definition are reflected on all pages using it after successful publish.

### 8.5 Agent-assisted asset insertion
1. User asks Agent to find or create an asset.
2. Agent presents candidates and source/license context.
3. User selects one.
4. System validates and saves it to Drive-backed Asset Library.
5. User inserts it into the current selection or Canvas.
6. Undo removes the insertion without deleting the saved asset unless the user separately deletes it.

