## 10. Google Drive storage proposal

Illustrative structure:

```text
My Portfolio/
├── Data/
│   └── portfolio-data (Google Sheets)
└── Website/
    ├── Site/
    │   └── site-manifest.json
    ├── Pages/
    │   ├── page-home.json
    │   └── page-about.json
    ├── Components/
    │   ├── Global/
    │   │   ├── Headers/
    │   │   └── Footers/
    │   ├── Local/
    │   │   └── {page-id}/
    │   └── Shared/
    ├── Templates/
    │   ├── Components/
    │   ├── Sections/
    │   ├── Headers/
    │   ├── Footers/
    │   ├── Pages/
    │   └── Sites/
    ├── Assets/
    │   ├── Images/
    │   ├── Logos/
    │   ├── Icons/
    │   ├── Illustrations/
    │   ├── Fonts/
    │   └── Other/
    └── Published/
        └── {immutable-build-id}/
```

This is a logical organization. Implementation may use Drive file metadata/appProperties and a manifest to avoid excessive folder traversal. Batch operations and caching are required to respect Google API quotas and latency.

Supabase must not store these records or their metadata.

