## 13. Acceptance criteria

### Element Library
- [ ] User can find supported elements by search and category.
- [ ] Each element has a recognizable icon and accessible text label.
- [ ] User can insert by drag-and-drop and click.
- [ ] Invalid nesting is prevented with clear feedback.
- [ ] Recently Used and Favorites work consistently.
- [ ] Panel works on Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile.

### Icon, Logo, and Assets
- [ ] Icon, Logo, and Image are distinct element types.
- [ ] User can search/select icons from supported libraries.
- [ ] User can upload and reuse logos from Asset Library.
- [ ] SVG is sanitized before use.
- [ ] Asset source/license metadata is retained when available.
- [ ] Agent asset insertion requires user approval.
- [ ] Canonical assets remain in user-owned Google Drive.

### Components and Templates
- [ ] User can save a selection as a Component or applicable Template.
- [ ] Saved items appear in the correct library.
- [ ] Inserting a saved template creates an editable instance.
- [ ] Independent instances do not silently change when the template changes.
- [ ] Linked component behavior is explicit and supports detach.
- [ ] Version/compatibility metadata is persisted.

### Header and Footer
- [ ] Each page can independently select Global, Local, or None for Header.
- [ ] Each page can independently select Global, Local, or None for Footer.
- [ ] New pages default to the site's configured Global layout.
- [ ] Local copy from Global is independent.
- [ ] Editing Local affects only its page.
- [ ] Editing Global affects all pages referencing that Global component after successful publish.
- [ ] Header/Footer can be saved as reusable templates.
- [ ] Responsive previews work at Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile.
- [ ] Publishing is atomic across all affected pages.
- [ ] Failed publish preserves the previous live site.

### Data and Security
- [ ] Portfolio data, component definitions, templates, and asset metadata are not stored in Supabase.
- [ ] Canonical source files are stored in user-owned Google Drive.
- [ ] Public rendering cannot access Builder credentials or OAuth tokens.
- [ ] Build validates missing component/asset references before activation.

