## 14. Implementation plan

Implement in dependency order, with production-quality validation at each stage.

| Phase | Scope | Exit condition |
|---|---|---|
| 1. Registry foundation | Element registry, metadata schema, icon mapping, nesting rules | Registry-driven panel works for existing elements |
| 2. Expanded catalog | Add catalog groups and core elements | Required categories are usable and tested |
| 3. Asset foundation | Drive-backed Asset Library, upload validation, icon/logo elements | Assets can be safely uploaded, selected, and reused |
| 4. Save/reuse system | Component save, template types, library UI, version metadata | User can save, browse, preview, and insert editable templates |
| 5. Header/Footer foundation | Global component definitions and page layout modes | Global/Local/None works for both slots |
| 6. Editor integration | Canvas labels, Page Settings, responsive editing | UX is clear across devices |
| 7. Publishing integration | Dependency validation, coherent build, atomic activation | No partial site activation; rollback works |
| 8. Agent asset workflow | Search/generate/approve/validate/insert | Agent workflow is safe, auditable, and recoverable |

Do not start with a large number of decorative elements before the registry, schema, asset handling, and publishing contracts are stable.

