## 16. Decisions to lock before implementation

The following choices should be resolved during technical design or a focused proof of concept:

1. Exact icon libraries and their licenses.
2. Whether linked reusable Components are included in the first implementation or all inserted instances are independent initially.
3. Revision policy for Global Components and linked instances.
4. Whether Header/Footer templates can include dynamic collection content.
5. Exact SVG sanitization library and accepted SVG feature subset.
6. Asset size/type limits and generated image variants.
7. Agent search providers and license/provenance requirements.
8. Whether multiple Global Header/Footer variants are supported at launch or one active variant per slot.

Recommended defaults:
- Start with one active Global Header and one active Global Footer, while allowing multiple saved templates.
- Make template insertion independent by default.
- Introduce linked reusable instances only with explicit UI and version-update controls.
- Use a curated icon library with verified licensing.
- Require approval before Agent inserts an asset.
- Keep all canonical portfolio data and assets in user-owned Google Drive.

